feat(mysql): deepen COM_QUERY compat — correlated subqueries, comparison ops, multi-aggregate GROUP BY, expression-based UPDATE SET

T038 progress: five new MySQL compatibility features implemented.

Engine:
- Add data_update_exprs() for per-row expression evaluation in UPDATE SET
  (salary = salary * 1.1 now evaluates the expression against each matching row)
- Existing data_update() delegates to data_update_exprs() via Expr::Lit wrapping

Server (MySQL compat layer):
- Correlated subquery in projection: detect outer table refs in subquery,
  add extra columns to outer projection for correlated values, substitute per row
- Binary comparison operators (>, <, >=, <=, =, !=, <>) in parse_sql_scalar_expr
- Multi-aggregate GROUP BY with ORDER BY: track per-aggregate column indices,
  include aggregate input columns in source SQL, add ORDER BY sorting
- Embedded subquery pre-evaluation in arithmetic expressions
  (salary - (SELECT AVG(salary) FROM users) pre-evaluates the subquery)
- SqlPlan::Update.set changed from BTreeMap<String, Lit> to BTreeMap<String, Expr>

Tests: 285 passing (204 unit + 29 integration + 52 other)
Corpus: 1657 lines, 677 statements — all TODO blocks resolved
